# Dalal — example environment configuration
#
# Copy to .env.local and replace the placeholders with real values.
#
#     cp .env.example .env.local
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NEVER COMMIT REAL VALUES.
#
# This file contains placeholders only and is the ONLY .env file tracked by
# git (see .gitignore). Real values are distributed out of band and set in
# Vercel per environment. See ARCHITECTURE.md §17.
#
# A leaked key requires ROTATION, not deleting the commit.
# TEAM.md rules 9 and 10.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


# --- Public configuration -------------------------------------------------
# Reaches the browser. Safe to expose ONLY because authorization is enforced
# at the data layer with default-deny policies (ARCHITECTURE.md §11, §17.1).
# If those policies were incomplete, this key would be an open door.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-public-anon-key-here


# --- Server-only secrets --------------------------------------------------
# MUST NEVER reach the browser. Must never be referenced in client-reachable
# code. Exposure bypasses every authorization policy in the system.
#
# ARCHITECTURE.md §17.3: under the current design the application should NOT
# need an elevated credential at all — reads and the bid operation run with
# the user's own identity, elevated writes happen inside the database, and
# the closing scheduler runs inside Supabase.
#
# The appearance of a service-role key in application configuration is a
# SIGNAL THAT SOMETHING HAS DRIFTED FROM THE ARCHITECTURE. Raise it with the
# team before adding one. The placeholder below is commented out for exactly
# that reason.

# SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=do-not-add-without-team-review


# --- Notes ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Variable names are prefixed so public and server-only values are
# distinguishable at a glance in review (ARCHITECTURE.md §17.2).
#
# Naming may be adjusted once the framework is chosen in Sprint 0 (S0-07);
# the public / server-only distinction must be preserved whatever the prefix.
#
# Add a new variable: announce it to the team, add its NAME here, then set
# the value in Vercel for every environment. TEAM.md rule 14.
